      "content": "High blood pressure, or hypertension, means your arteries have too much pressure inside them. This often is felt in silence, but can harm your heart or brain over time. Avoid heart speaks or strokes by staying on a good diet, moving more, and following your healthcare provider's advice. High numbers usually don’t show signs, but they're bad news for you. Getting regular checks is key to catching and handling this sneaky health foe.",
